  "notes": [
    "Direct exact-greedy search completed all 18,944 preregistered environment training hands and passed the mechanism gate; candidate frozen before validation.",
    "Frozen candidate and untouched source validation raw streams align on every pair index and deck; only the two actor bias tensors differ."
  ],
  "result": {
    "summary": "A one-pass exact-greedy coordinate search used 18,944 physical environment training hands and selected four Standard10 actor-bias offsets with positive robust search score. On 10,240 untouched validation hands, only 2/5 paired deltas were positive, none had a positive lower bound, and pooled candidate-minus-source was -7.5016 bb/100 (95% CI [-25.9172,10.9141]).",
    "conclusion": "Direct tournament outcomes can change deployed learned weights and greedy behavior without PPO, but this 18-dimensional bias-only objective overfit its 64-pair search streams and did not generalize to unseen policies/deals. The failure is not an execution or optimizer ambiguity: mixed observation contracts, hashes, raw pairs, tensor scope, and training-hand accounting all passed. Increasing coordinate passes or tuning only step size would amplify the same weak objective and is not justified.",
    "decision": "REJECT_BIAS_ONLY_DIRECT_GREEDY_SEARCH",
    "next_step": "Retire global bias coordinate search. The remaining high-information route is a state-conditioned objective with reliable alternative-action credit and broad independent data, or a materially broader/deeper solver teacher; do not reuse fixed internal anchor panels as a promotion proxy and do not allocate Slumbot to this candidate."
  },
